#: ../../technical/topics/persistence-and-secure-storage.md
msgid "Topic summary"
msgstr "Resumen del tema"

#: ../../technical/topics/persistence-and-secure-storage.md:10
msgid ""
"Profile facts, transactions, calculations, filings and evidence live "
"primarily in bucket-scoped encrypted SQL secure objects. Registered "
"namespaces define sensitivity, schema and custody policy. AES-GCM binds "
"ciphertext to namespace/key/schema; HMAC keys hide natural identifiers; "
"revision-guarded batches and parent checks keep related records "
"consistent. A plaintext transaction-date routing index exposes date/ID "
"metadata but falls back to encrypted scan if incomplete. [Full synthesis"
"](persistence-and-secure-storage.md), write funnel "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/sql/_secure_object_writes.py`),"
" date fallback "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/profile/transactions.py`), "
"[detail](../articles/019-profile-persistence-for-transactions-review-"
"exchange-and-workflows.md), [detail](../articles/025-encrypted-sql-"
"repository-revision-writes-and-workflow-storage.md)."
msgstr ""
"Los datos del perfil, transacciones, cálculos, declaraciones y evidencias"
" residen principalmente en objetos seguros SQL cifrados delimitados al "
"contenedor. Los espacios de nombres registrados definen sensibilidad, "
"esquema y política de custodia. AES-GCM vincula el texto cifrado al "
"espacio de nombres, clave y esquema; las claves HMAC ocultan "
"identificadores naturales; los lotes protegidos por revisión y las "
"comprobaciones de padres mantienen coherentes los registros relacionados."
" Un índice de encaminamiento por fecha de transacción en texto claro "
"expone metadatos de fecha e identificador, pero recurre al examen cifrado"
" si está incompleto. [Síntesis completa](persistence-and-secure-"
"storage.md), canal de escritura "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/sql/_secure_object_writes.py`),"
" alternativa por fechas "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/profile/transactions.py`), "
"[detalle](../articles/019-profile-persistence-for-transactions-review-"
"exchange-and-workflows.md), [detalle](../articles/025-encrypted-sql-"
"repository-revision-writes-and-workflow-storage.md)."

#: ../../technical/topics/persistence-and-secure-storage.md:12
msgid ""
"Profile DEKs are password/recovery wrapped, sentinel-proven and housed in"
" no-replace published capsules; KDF work runs in a bounded supervised "
"child. Session acceleration splits an OS-keychain random key from an "
"encrypted receipt. Automation credentials use native stores and durable "
"denial intents. Attachments and archives retain encrypted bytes with "
"digest checks. An operation journal validates ordered history and exact "
"lease ownership; consent history appends before off-host evidence "
"dispatch without retaining document bytes. Capsule "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/custody/capsule.py`), "
"acceleration "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/custody/acceleration_receipt.py`),"
" consent ledger "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/llm/consent_ledger.py`), "
"[detail](../articles/017-persistence-for-llm-records-durable-operations-"
"and-profile-state.md), [detail](../articles/021-supervised-key-"
"derivation-and-automation-custody.md), [detail](../articles/022-profile-"
"capsule-lifecycle-and-custody-proof.md)."
msgstr ""
"Las DEK de perfiles se envuelven mediante contraseña y recuperación, se "
"acreditan mediante un centinela y se alojan en cápsulas publicadas sin "
"sustitución; el trabajo de KDF se ejecuta en un proceso hijo supervisado "
"y acotado. La aceleración de sesiones separa una clave aleatoria en el "
"llavero del sistema operativo de un recibo cifrado. Las credenciales de "
"automatización utilizan almacenes nativos e intenciones duraderas de "
"denegación. Los adjuntos y archivos conservan bytes cifrados con "
"comprobaciones de resumen. Un diario de operaciones valida el historial "
"ordenado y la titularidad exacta de concesiones temporales; el historial "
"de consentimiento se amplía antes de enviar evidencias fuera del equipo "
"sin conservar los bytes del documento. Cápsula "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/custody/capsule.py`), "
"aceleración "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/custody/acceleration_receipt.py`),"
" registro de consentimiento "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/llm/consent_ledger.py`), "
"[detalle](../articles/017-persistence-for-llm-records-durable-operations-"
"and-profile-state.md), [detalle](../articles/021-supervised-key-"
"derivation-and-automation-custody.md), [detalle](../articles/022-profile-"
"capsule-lifecycle-and-custody-proof.md)."

#: ../../technical/topics/persistence-and-secure-storage.md:14
msgid ""
"Scoped risks include direct in-place financial checkpoint writes, a "
"potentially racing attachment manifest read/merge/write, database content"
" omitted from deletion-inventory digests, and outer review-package "
"metadata absent from this adapter's AEAD associated data pending "
"signature tracing. SQL revision hashes are unkeyed and cover a declared "
"subset of fields. SQLite WAL `synchronous=NORMAL` permits last-"
"transaction loss on power failure; no crash test or arbitrary-old-schema "
"migration was established. Checkpoint "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/operations/financial_operand_custody.py`),"
" attachment merge "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/attachment.py`), inventory "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/custody/_inventory.py`), AEAD "
"context "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/profile/review_package_recipient_encryption.py`),"
" [detail](../articles/020-encrypted-blobs-bucket-archives-and-custody-"
"filesystem.md), [detail](../articles/024-profile-custody-adapter-storage-"
"routing-and-secure-object-contracts.md)."
msgstr ""
"Los riesgos acotados incluyen escrituras directas sobre el propio archivo"
" de puntos de control financieros, una lectura, combinación y escritura "
"del manifiesto de adjuntos potencialmente sujeta a carreras, contenido de"
" base de datos omitido de los resúmenes del inventario de eliminación y "
"metadatos externos de paquetes de revisión ausentes de los datos "
"asociados AEAD de este adaptador, pendientes de rastrear la firma. Los "
"hashes de revisión SQL no tienen clave y cubren un subconjunto declarado "
"de campos. SQLite WAL con `synchronous=NORMAL` permite perder la última "
"transacción ante un corte de energía; no se acreditaron pruebas de fallos"
" ni migración desde esquemas antiguos arbitrarios. Punto de control "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/operations/financial_operand_custody.py`),"
" combinación de adjuntos "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/attachment.py`), inventario "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/custody/_inventory.py`), "
"contexto AEAD "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/profile/review_package_recipient_encryption.py`),"
" [detalle](../articles/020-encrypted-blobs-bucket-archives-and-custody-"
"filesystem.md), [detalle](../articles/024-profile-custody-adapter-"
"storage-routing-and-secure-object-contracts.md)."

#: ../../technical/topics/persistence-and-secure-storage.md:16
msgid ""
"These are persistence-layer observations. A caller's journal, lock, "
"signature verification or recovery step may narrow the practical impact; "
"each path needs its full composition traced before it is described as an "
"end-to-end failure. The stated confidentiality guarantees also rely on "
"native key-store and filesystem permissions outside these SQL adapters."
msgstr ""
"Son observaciones de la capa de persistencia. El diario, bloqueo, "
"verificación de firmas o paso de recuperación de quien llama puede "
"limitar la repercusión práctica; debe rastrearse la composición completa "
"de cada ruta antes de describirla como un fallo de extremo a extremo. Las"
" garantías declaradas de confidencialidad también dependen de permisos "
"del almacén nativo de claves y del sistema de archivos ajenos a estos "
"adaptadores SQL."

#: ../../technical/topics/persistence-and-secure-storage.md:22
msgid "Storage model and capability"
msgstr "Modelo de almacenamiento y capacidades"

#: ../../technical/topics/persistence-and-secure-storage.md:24
msgid ""
"Private product state is primarily stored as profile-bound encrypted "
"secure objects in SQLite, with separate filesystem custody for profile "
"key capsules, attachments, archives, native secret handles and durable "
"operation journals. Namespace definitions declare owner, sensitivity, "
"schema and custody/mirror policy. A `BucketSession` retains one profile "
"DEK, deadlines and a bucket-routed database engine; closing it wipes its "
"mutable key buffer and disposes the engine. SQL rows use HMAC-addressed "
"object identities and AES-GCM associated data for namespace, key digest "
"and schema version. The database also has a plaintext, rebuildable "
"transaction date index containing routing dates and record IDs; missing "
"or incomplete index rows trigger encrypted-scan fallback, so it is "
"metadata with a different confidentiality posture from the transaction "
"content. Namespace registry "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/secure_object_namespaces.py`),"
" bucket session "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/master_key/bucket_session.py`),"
" SQL row model (`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/sql/orm.py`), "
"date fallback "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/profile/transactions.py`), "
"[analyses](../articles/019-profile-persistence-for-transactions-review-"
"exchange-and-workflows.md), [analysis](../articles/023-profile-custody-"
"primitives-session-state-and-secure-envelopes.md), "
"[analysis](../articles/024-profile-custody-adapter-storage-routing-and-"
"secure-object-contracts.md), [analysis](../articles/025-encrypted-sql-"
"repository-revision-writes-and-workflow-storage.md)."
msgstr ""
"El estado privado del producto se almacena principalmente como objetos "
"seguros cifrados vinculados al perfil en SQLite, con custodia separada en"
" el sistema de archivos para cápsulas de claves de perfil, adjuntos, "
"archivos, referencias nativas de secretos y diarios duraderos de "
"operaciones. Las definiciones de espacios de nombres declaran "
"propietario, sensibilidad, esquema y política de custodia y réplica. Una "
"`BucketSession` retiene una DEK de perfil, plazos y un motor de base de "
"datos dirigido al contenedor; cerrarla borra su búfer mutable de clave y "
"libera el motor. Las filas SQL utilizan identidades de objetos "
"direccionadas por HMAC y datos asociados AES-GCM para espacio de nombres,"
" resumen de clave y versión de esquema. La base de datos también tiene un"
" índice reconstruible de fechas de transacción en texto claro con fechas "
"de encaminamiento e identificadores de registros; las filas de índice "
"ausentes o incompletas activan la alternativa de examen cifrado, por lo "
"que son metadatos con una situación de confidencialidad distinta del "
"contenido de las transacciones. Registro de espacios de nombres "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/secure_object_namespaces.py`),"
" sesión del contenedor "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/master_key/bucket_session.py`),"
" modelo de filas SQL "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/sql/orm.py`), alternativa por "
"fechas (`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/profile/transactions.py`), "
"[análisis](../articles/019-profile-persistence-for-transactions-review-"
"exchange-and-workflows.md), [análisis](../articles/023-profile-custody-"
"primitives-session-state-and-secure-envelopes.md), "
"[análisis](../articles/024-profile-custody-adapter-storage-routing-and-"
"secure-object-contracts.md), [análisis](../articles/025-encrypted-sql-"
"repository-revision-writes-and-workflow-storage.md)."

#: ../../technical/topics/persistence-and-secure-storage.md:26
msgid ""
"The secure-object write funnel validates registered "
"namespace/classification, encrypts payloads with identity AAD, derives "
"deterministic revision IDs, checks expected revisions and commits batch "
"writes/deletions with read assertions in one SQL transaction. Profile "
"repositories use those revisions for compare-and-swap mutations, parent "
"validation and related event co-commits. Invoice creation joins catalogue"
" and bucket event; calculation revisions are validated against pinned "
"authority and work units; verification reports require their calculation "
"parent; official and pending-local observations remain separate layers; "
"withholding windows co-commit head, generation, idempotency and source-"
"liability guards. The transaction catalogue encrypts individual rows plus"
" membership index, and checks its plaintext date route against that "
"encrypted membership before trusting it. These mechanisms reduce lost "
"updates and misleading cross-record reads, though actual isolation and "
"crash behavior were not exercised. SQL writes "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/sql/_secure_object_writes.py`),"
" invoice co-commit "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/profile/catalogue_creation.py`), "
"verification parent "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/profile/modelos_verification_reports.py`),"
" withholding workflow "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/profile/withholding_observation_workflow.py`),"
" transaction catalogue "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/profile/transactions.py`), "
"[analyses](../articles/017-persistence-for-llm-records-durable-"
"operations-and-profile-state.md), [analysis](../articles/018-profile-"
"persistence-for-invoices-filings-and-calculation-evidence.md), "
"[analysis](../articles/019-profile-persistence-for-transactions-review-"
"exchange-and-workflows.md), [analysis](../articles/025-encrypted-sql-"
"repository-revision-writes-and-workflow-storage.md)."
msgstr ""
"El canal de escritura de objetos seguros valida el espacio de nombres y "
"la clasificación registrados, cifra cargas con AAD de identidad, deriva "
"identificadores deterministas de revisión, comprueba revisiones esperadas"
" y confirma escrituras y eliminaciones por lotes con aserciones de "
"lectura en una transacción SQL. Los repositorios de perfiles utilizan "
"esas revisiones para modificaciones de comparación e intercambio, "
"validación de padres y confirmaciones conjuntas de eventos relacionados. "
"La creación de facturas une catálogo y evento del contenedor; las "
"revisiones de cálculo se validan frente a autoridad fijada y unidades de "
"trabajo; los informes de verificación exigen su cálculo padre; las "
"observaciones oficiales y locales pendientes permanecen en capas "
"separadas; las ventanas de retenciones confirman conjuntamente cabecera, "
"generación, idempotencia y controles de obligaciones de origen. El "
"catálogo de transacciones cifra filas individuales y un índice de "
"pertenencia y comprueba su ruta de fechas en texto claro frente a esa "
"pertenencia cifrada antes de confiar en ella. Estos mecanismos reducen "
"actualizaciones perdidas y lecturas engañosas entre registros, aunque no "
"se ejercitaron el aislamiento real ni el comportamiento ante fallos. "
"Escrituras SQL "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/sql/_secure_object_writes.py`),"
" confirmación conjunta de facturas "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/profile/catalogue_creation.py`), padre"
" de verificación "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/profile/modelos_verification_reports.py`),"
" flujo de retenciones "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/profile/withholding_observation_workflow.py`),"
" catálogo de transacciones "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/profile/transactions.py`), "
"[análisis](../articles/017-persistence-for-llm-records-durable-"
"operations-and-profile-state.md), [análisis](../articles/018-profile-"
"persistence-for-invoices-filings-and-calculation-evidence.md), "
"[análisis](../articles/019-profile-persistence-for-transactions-review-"
"exchange-and-workflows.md), [análisis](../articles/025-encrypted-sql-"
"repository-revision-writes-and-workflow-storage.md)."

#: ../../technical/topics/persistence-and-secure-storage.md:28
msgid ""
"An operation journal stores a credential-free current snapshot and "
"ordered history with contiguous sequence, monotonic timestamps and "
"terminal-state consistency. Leases share its lock and require exact "
"ownership for commits. Sensitive operation operands are stored separately"
" as content-addressed encrypted objects and re-hashed on resolution. LLM "
"cache, usage and run records occupy encrypted diagnostic namespaces with "
"age/count retention; the cache avoids persisting a redaction-altered "
"response. Off-host evidence consent history is different: it records "
"content address, provider/model, surface and time, appends before "
"dispatch and has no pruning path, because later withdrawal analysis needs"
" history. This is audit metadata, not a copy of transmitted bytes or "
"prompts. Journal validation "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/operations/_journal_validation.py`), "
"leases (`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/operations/lease.py`), operand "
"custody "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/operations/secure_references.py`), LLM"
" cache (`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/llm/cache.py`), consent ledger "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/llm/consent_ledger.py`), "
"[analysis](../articles/017-persistence-for-llm-records-durable-"
"operations-and-profile-state.md)."
msgstr ""
"Un diario de operaciones almacena una instantánea actual sin credenciales"
" y un historial ordenado con secuencia contigua, marcas temporales "
"monótonas y coherencia de estados terminales. Las concesiones temporales "
"comparten su bloqueo y exigen titularidad exacta para las confirmaciones."
" Los operandos sensibles de operaciones se almacenan por separado como "
"objetos cifrados direccionados por contenido y se vuelve a calcular su "
"hash al resolverlos. La caché LLM, el uso y los registros de ejecución "
"ocupan espacios de nombres cifrados de diagnóstico con conservación por "
"antigüedad y cantidad; la caché evita persistir una respuesta alterada "
"por ocultación de datos. El historial de consentimiento de evidencias "
"fuera del equipo es distinto: registra dirección de contenido, proveedor "
"y modelo, superficie y hora, añade antes del despacho y no tiene ruta de "
"poda porque el análisis de retirada posterior necesita historial. Son "
"metadatos de auditoría, no una copia de los bytes o instrucciones "
"transmitidos. Validación del diario "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/operations/_journal_validation.py`), "
"concesiones temporales "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/operations/lease.py`), custodia de "
"operandos "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/operations/secure_references.py`), "
"caché LLM (`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/llm/cache.py`), registro de "
"consentimiento "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/llm/consent_ledger.py`), "
"[análisis](../articles/017-persistence-for-llm-records-durable-"
"operations-and-profile-state.md)."

#: ../../technical/topics/persistence-and-secure-storage.md:30
msgid "Key custody and recovery"
msgstr "Custodia de claves y recuperación"

#: ../../technical/topics/persistence-and-secure-storage.md:32
msgid ""
"Profile registration generates a DEK wrapped by a password-derived key "
"and writes an encrypted sentinel proving that an unwrapped key belongs to"
" the claimed profile and epoch. Recovery is optional and wraps the same "
"DEK under an independently derived, high-entropy code. KDF work runs in a"
" fresh supervised child with bounded frames, an Argon2id parameter grid, "
"pre-secret readiness attestation and process/resource containment; "
"malformed or timed-out work has no in-process fallback. Capsules are "
"staged as complete sibling directories, write a commit marker last, then "
"publish with a no-replace rename. Discovery accepts only canonical UUID "
"directories and current markers; retired plaintext layouts are refused. "
"Rotation requires a direct predecessor and same DEK epoch; deletion uses "
"a transaction marker, tombstone and inventory witness. "
"Registration/recovery "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/profile_custody.py`), sentinel"
" "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/custody/sentinel_contract.py`),"
" KDF worker "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/custody/_kdf_worker.py`), "
"capsule publication "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/custody/capsule.py`), rotation"
" (`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/custody/capsule.py`), "
"[analyses](../articles/020-encrypted-blobs-bucket-archives-and-custody-"
"filesystem.md), [analysis](../articles/021-supervised-key-derivation-and-"
"automation-custody.md), [analysis](../articles/022-profile-capsule-"
"lifecycle-and-custody-proof.md), [analysis](../articles/023-profile-"
"custody-primitives-session-state-and-secure-envelopes.md), "
"[analysis](../articles/024-profile-custody-adapter-storage-routing-and-"
"secure-object-contracts.md)."
msgstr ""
"El registro de perfiles genera una DEK envuelta por una clave derivada de"
" contraseña y escribe un centinela cifrado que demuestra que una clave "
"desenvuelta pertenece al perfil y época declarados. La recuperación es "
"opcional y envuelve la misma DEK bajo un código de alta entropía derivado"
" independientemente. El trabajo de KDF se ejecuta en un proceso hijo "
"nuevo y supervisado con tramas acotadas, una cuadrícula de parámetros "
"Argon2id, atestación de preparación anterior al secreto y contención de "
"procesos y recursos; el trabajo mal formado o que agota el plazo no tiene"
" alternativa dentro del proceso. Las cápsulas se preparan como "
"directorios hermanos completos, escriben al final un marcador de "
"confirmación y después se publican mediante renombrado sin sustitución. "
"El descubrimiento solo acepta directorios UUID canónicos y marcadores "
"actuales; se rechazan diseños retirados en texto claro. La rotación exige"
" un predecesor directo y la misma época de DEK; la eliminación utiliza un"
" marcador de transacción, una marca de eliminación y un testigo de "
"inventario. Registro y recuperación "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/profile_custody.py`), "
"centinela "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/custody/sentinel_contract.py`),"
" proceso KDF "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/custody/_kdf_worker.py`), "
"publicación de cápsulas "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/custody/capsule.py`), rotación"
" (`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/custody/capsule.py`), "
"[análisis](../articles/020-encrypted-blobs-bucket-archives-and-custody-"
"filesystem.md), [análisis](../articles/021-supervised-key-derivation-and-"
"automation-custody.md), [análisis](../articles/022-profile-capsule-"
"lifecycle-and-custody-proof.md), [análisis](../articles/023-profile-"
"custody-primitives-session-state-and-secure-envelopes.md), "
"[análisis](../articles/024-profile-custody-adapter-storage-routing-and-"
"secure-object-contracts.md)."

#: ../../technical/topics/persistence-and-secure-storage.md:34
msgid ""
"Human login acceleration splits a random key in the OS keychain from an "
"encrypted receipt in the profile keystore, with authenticated "
"profile/session/generation/epoch/deadline metadata. Exact-byte journals "
"recover interrupted receipt swaps. Automation keys and grant wrapping "
"material use explicitly selected native secret stores, anchored control-"
"file publication and durable denial before optional native cleanup. The "
"design accepts the OS account as a trust boundary; it does not claim "
"defense against another equally privileged process. Memory wiping covers "
"mutable buffers, not all Python or native copies. The login throttle "
"intentionally fails open if its revocable local sidecar is missing or "
"corrupt, favoring availability over resistance to a local actor who can "
"disrupt it. Acceleration receipt "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/custody/acceleration_receipt.py`),"
" automation store "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/custody/automation_store.py`),"
" session close "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/master_key/bucket_session.py`),"
" throttle "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/master_key/login_throttle.py`),"
" [analyses](../articles/021-supervised-key-derivation-and-automation-"
"custody.md), [analysis](../articles/023-profile-custody-primitives-"
"session-state-and-secure-envelopes.md)."
msgstr ""
"La aceleración del inicio de sesión humano separa una clave aleatoria en "
"el llavero del sistema operativo de un recibo cifrado en el almacén de "
"claves del perfil, con metadatos autenticados de perfil, sesión, "
"generación, época y plazo. Los diarios de bytes exactos recuperan "
"intercambios de recibos interrumpidos. Las claves de automatización y el "
"material de envoltura de autorizaciones utilizan almacenes nativos de "
"secretos seleccionados expresamente, publicación anclada de archivos de "
"control y denegación duradera antes de una limpieza nativa opcional. El "
"diseño acepta la cuenta del sistema operativo como límite de confianza; "
"no afirma defenderse de otro proceso con los mismos privilegios. El "
"borrado de memoria abarca búferes mutables, no todas las copias Python o "
"nativas. La limitación del inicio de sesión falla intencionadamente de "
"forma permisiva si su archivo auxiliar local revocable falta o está "
"corrupto, priorizando disponibilidad frente a resistencia a un actor "
"local que pueda alterarlo. Recibo de aceleración "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/custody/acceleration_receipt.py`),"
" almacén de automatización "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/custody/automation_store.py`),"
" cierre de sesión "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/master_key/bucket_session.py`),"
" limitación "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/master_key/login_throttle.py`),"
" [análisis](../articles/021-supervised-key-derivation-and-automation-"
"custody.md), [análisis](../articles/023-profile-custody-primitives-"
"session-state-and-secure-envelopes.md)."

#: ../../technical/topics/persistence-and-secure-storage.md:36
msgid ""
"Attachments are encrypted content-addressed blobs with encrypted "
"manifests. Reads recheck bucket ownership, digest, size and row identity;"
" duplicate ingestion merges links. A separate filesystem blob store "
"encrypts non-CORPUS classifications and checks ciphertext and plaintext "
"digests. Portable archives have strict versioned members and staged "
"publication; archive data remains encrypted. These are real "
"confidentiality and integrity measures, with bounded exceptions: "
"attachment manifest merge reads before its optional writer fence and "
"passes no local revision witness, so caller serialization must prevent "
"concurrent lost links; a blob/manifest pair spans two files and can "
"become mismatched after sudden termination; the archive reader "
"materializes all tar members before rejecting a noncanonical member "
"count. Attachment store "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/attachment.py`), manifest "
"merge (`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/attachment.py`), blob "
"store "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/blob_store/blob_store.py`), "
"archive reader "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/bucket/sealed_archive_reader.py`),"
" [analysis](../articles/020-encrypted-blobs-bucket-archives-and-custody-"
"filesystem.md)."
msgstr ""
"Los adjuntos son blobs cifrados direccionados por contenido con "
"manifiestos cifrados. Las lecturas vuelven a comprobar titularidad del "
"contenedor, resumen, tamaño e identidad de fila; la recepción duplicada "
"combina vínculos. Un almacén separado de blobs en el sistema de archivos "
"cifra clasificaciones distintas de CORPUS y comprueba resúmenes de texto "
"cifrado y texto claro. Los archivos portátiles tienen miembros estrictos "
"versionados y publicación preparada; los datos del archivo permanecen "
"cifrados. Son medidas reales de confidencialidad e integridad, con "
"excepciones acotadas: la combinación del manifiesto de adjuntos lee antes"
" de su barrera opcional de escritura y no pasa un testigo local de "
"revisión, por lo que la serialización de quien llama debe evitar pérdida "
"concurrente de vínculos; un par blob y manifiesto abarca dos archivos y "
"puede quedar desajustado tras una terminación repentina; el lector de "
"archivos materializa todos los miembros tar antes de rechazar un recuento"
" no canónico de miembros. Almacén de adjuntos "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/attachment.py`), combinación "
"de manifiestos "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/attachment.py`), almacén de "
"blobs "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/blob_store/blob_store.py`), "
"lector de archivos "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/bucket/sealed_archive_reader.py`),"
" [análisis](../articles/020-encrypted-blobs-bucket-archives-and-custody-"
"filesystem.md)."

#: ../../technical/topics/persistence-and-secure-storage.md:38
msgid "Scoped quality and assurance limits"
msgstr "Calidad acotada y límites de garantía"

#: ../../technical/topics/persistence-and-secure-storage.md:40
msgid ""
"Several integrity boundaries deserve precise language. SQL revision IDs "
"are unkeyed hashes over a declared subset of columns; they detect "
"inconsistent rows but do not authenticate arbitrary database edits or "
"cover all ancestry/provenance metadata. Review-package recipient AEAD "
"locally binds the recipient key but not the outer expiry, replay nonce or"
" review-only flags; a higher-level signature may cover the envelope, so "
"impact requires tracing package verification. Financial-operand "
"checkpoints use direct in-place `write_text`, unlike the atomic journal "
"writer, and could be unreadable after interruption. Deletion inventory "
"binds ordinary custody file bytes but only database presence by path, "
"leaving concurrent database content changes outside its witness. The "
"secret store checks expiry presence on write but `get` does not itself "
"reject an expired value; consumer checks remain to be verified. Revision "
"coverage "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/sql/secure_object_crypto.py`),"
" recipient AEAD "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/profile/review_package_recipient_encryption.py`),"
" checkpoint write "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/operations/financial_operand_custody.py`),"
" inventory "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/custody/_inventory.py`), "
"secret-store get "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/secret_store/store.py`), "
"[analyses](../articles/017-persistence-for-llm-records-durable-"
"operations-and-profile-state.md), [analysis](../articles/019-profile-"
"persistence-for-transactions-review-exchange-and-workflows.md), "
"[analysis](../articles/020-encrypted-blobs-bucket-archives-and-custody-"
"filesystem.md), [analysis](../articles/024-profile-custody-adapter-"
"storage-routing-and-secure-object-contracts.md), "
"[analysis](../articles/025-encrypted-sql-repository-revision-writes-and-"
"workflow-storage.md)."
msgstr ""
"Varios límites de integridad merecen lenguaje preciso. Los "
"identificadores de revisión SQL son hashes sin clave de un subconjunto "
"declarado de columnas; detectan filas incoherentes, pero no autentican "
"ediciones arbitrarias de la base de datos ni cubren todos los metadatos "
"de ascendencia y procedencia. El AEAD del destinatario de paquetes de "
"revisión vincula localmente la clave del destinatario, pero no la "
"caducidad externa, el nonce de repetición ni los indicadores de solo "
"revisión; una firma de nivel superior puede cubrir la envoltura, por lo "
"que la repercusión exige rastrear la verificación del paquete. Los puntos"
" de control de operandos financieros utilizan `write_text` directo sobre "
"el propio archivo, a diferencia del escritor atómico del diario, y "
"podrían quedar ilegibles tras una interrupción. El inventario de "
"eliminación vincula bytes de archivos ordinarios de custodia, pero solo "
"la presencia de la base de datos por ruta, dejando cambios concurrentes "
"de contenido de la base de datos fuera de su testigo. El almacén de "
"secretos comprueba la presencia de caducidad al escribir, pero `get` no "
"rechaza por sí mismo un valor caducado; quedan por verificar las "
"comprobaciones de quienes consumen los datos. Cobertura de revisión "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/sql/secure_object_crypto.py`),"
" AEAD del destinatario "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/profile/review_package_recipient_encryption.py`),"
" escritura de puntos de control "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/operations/financial_operand_custody.py`),"
" inventario "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/custody/_inventory.py`), "
"consulta del almacén de secretos "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/secret_store/store.py`), "
"[análisis](../articles/017-persistence-for-llm-records-durable-"
"operations-and-profile-state.md), [análisis](../articles/019-profile-"
"persistence-for-transactions-review-exchange-and-workflows.md), "
"[análisis](../articles/020-encrypted-blobs-bucket-archives-and-custody-"
"filesystem.md), [análisis](../articles/024-profile-custody-adapter-"
"storage-routing-and-secure-object-contracts.md), "
"[análisis](../articles/025-encrypted-sql-repository-revision-writes-and-"
"workflow-storage.md)."

#: ../../technical/topics/persistence-and-secure-storage.md:42
msgid ""
"SQLite uses WAL and `synchronous=NORMAL`, explicitly allowing loss of the"
" most recent transaction on OS/power failure while preserving database "
"integrity. `create_all` establishes current tables, not a proven upgrade "
"path for arbitrary older databases. Replay-nonce history is append-only "
"without expiry and can grow, while classified namespace/custody rules "
"govern which records can be mirrored or exported. Runtime tests, power-"
"loss recovery, native keychain behavior, cryptographic deployment and "
"current legal correctness were not established by this static review. "
"Engine settings "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/sql/engine.py`), replay nonce "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/profile/recipient_replay_guard.py`), "
"namespace taxonomy "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/namespace_taxonomy.py`), "
"[analyses](../articles/018-profile-persistence-for-invoices-filings-and-"
"calculation-evidence.md), [analysis](../articles/025-encrypted-sql-"
"repository-revision-writes-and-workflow-storage.md)."
msgstr ""
"SQLite utiliza WAL y `synchronous=NORMAL`, lo que permite expresamente "
"perder la transacción más reciente ante un fallo del sistema operativo o "
"de energía mientras conserva la integridad de la base de datos. "
"`create_all` establece las tablas actuales, no una ruta de actualización "
"probada para bases antiguas arbitrarias. El historial de nonces de "
"repetición solo admite adiciones sin caducidad y puede crecer, mientras "
"que las reglas de clasificación de espacios de nombres y custodia rigen "
"qué registros pueden replicarse o exportarse. Esta revisión estática no "
"acreditó pruebas en ejecución, recuperación tras pérdida de energía, "
"comportamiento de llaveros nativos, despliegue criptográfico ni "
"corrección jurídica actual. Ajustes del motor "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/sql/engine.py`), nonce de "
"repetición "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/profile/recipient_replay_guard.py`), "
"taxonomía de espacios de nombres "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/persistence/storage/namespace_taxonomy.py`), "
"[análisis](../articles/018-profile-persistence-for-invoices-filings-and-"
"calculation-evidence.md), [análisis](../articles/025-encrypted-sql-"
"repository-revision-writes-and-workflow-storage.md)."

